{
  "sn35.74:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.74 ",
  "sn35.74:0.2": "8. Sick ",
  "sn35.74:0.3": "Sick (1st) ",
  "sn35.74:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn35.74:1.2": "Then a mendicant went up to the Buddha, and said to him, ",
  "sn35.74:1.3": "“Sir, in such-and-such monastery there’s a mendicant who is junior and not well-known. He’s sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "sn35.74:1.4": "Please go to him out of sympathy.” ",
  "sn35.74:2.1": "When the Buddha heard that the mendicant was junior and ill, understanding that he was not well-known, he went to him. ",
  "sn35.74:2.2": "That mendicant saw the Buddha coming off in the distance ",
  "sn35.74:2.3": "and stirred in his cot. ",
  "sn35.74:2.4": "The Buddha said to that monk, ",
  "sn35.74:2.5": "“It’s all right, mendicant, don’t get up. ",
  "sn35.74:2.6": "There are some seats spread out, I will sit there.” ",
  "sn35.74:2.7": "He sat down on the seat spread out ",
  "sn35.74:2.8": "and said to the mendicant, ",
  "sn35.74:2.9": "“I hope you’re keeping well, mendicant, I hope you’re all right. I hope your pain is fading, not growing; that its fading is evident, not its growing.” ",
  "sn35.74:3.1": "“Sir, I’m not keeping well, I’m not getting by. My pain is terrible and growing, not fading; its growing is evident, not its fading.” ",
  "sn35.74:4.1": "“I hope you don’t have any remorse or regret?” ",
  "sn35.74:5.1": "“Indeed, sir, I have no little remorse and regret.” ",
